    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0737" n="675" xml:id="pg675"/>

                <head>No. 381.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Zamacona to Mr.
                    Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Mexico in the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1878-05-06"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>
                            6, 1878</date>. (Received May 6.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am informed by the note of your
                    Department, dated the 4th instant, that the Chief Magistrate of this republic
                    will vouchsafe to receive me to-morrow at noon, affording me occasion to present
                    to him my credentials as envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of the
                    Government of Mexico.</p>
                <p>Availing myself of the benevolent invitation which the same note contains, I
                    shall be in your Department shortly before the ceremony, in order to be
                    conducted to the mansion of His Excellency the President.</p>
                <p>I avail, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>M. DE ZAMACOSTA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
